tags: party_affairs

= Campaigning

Election or not, the party is always trying to win new voters. Who should we focus our campaign on?

- @workers: Workers and employees, our traditional base.
- @new_middle: The educated urban middle class of professionals and public servants.
- @old_middle: The self-employed, small business owners and craftspeople.
- @rural: People in small towns and the countryside, who feel left behind.
- @unemployed: The unemployed and people on Grundsicherung.
- @catholics: East Germans, many of whom no longer trust any of the old parties.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@workers
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); workers_spd -= 2 if unemployment_rate >= 8; workers_spd -= 2 if unemployment_rate >= 11; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent) if investment_adopted = 1; resources -= 1; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress >= 1;

We campaign at factory gates, in union halls and in the new logistics centres. [? if unemployment_rate >= 8: With unemployment this high, our message is a harder sell. ?][? if investment_adopted = 1 : The Zukunftsprogramm gives us something concrete to offer. ?]

@new_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: new_middle_spd += 6*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd -= 4 if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0; resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1;

We campaign in university towns and city neighbourhoods, where the Grüne are our main rivals. [? if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0: Many here see us as old-fashioned. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: Our broader image makes it easier. ?]

@old_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: old_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; old_middle_spd -= 3 if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0; peoples_party_support += 1

We campaign among craftspeople and small business owners. [? if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0: Many of them have drifted to the AfD, and are hard to reach. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: Our broader image makes it easier. ?]

@rural
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: rural_spd += 5*(1-dissent); rural_spd -= 3*(1-dissent) if peoples_party == 0; resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1; rural_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if rural_policy >= 2

We campaign in small towns and villages, where the bus comes twice a day and the last doctor has retired. [? if peoples_party == 0: Many here see us as a party of the cities. ?][? if peoples_party > 0: Our broader image makes it easier. ?][? if rural_policy >= 2 : Our rural policies give us something to show. ?]

@unemployed
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; unemployed_spd -= 3 if welfare < 0; unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent) if investment_adopted = 1; unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare >= 2;

We campaign in job centres and poorer neighbourhoods, where turnout is lowest. [? if welfare < 0: After the benefit cuts, many here see us as part of the problem. ?][? if investment_adopted = 1 : The Zukunftsprogramm gives us something concrete to offer. ?]

@catholics
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: catholics_spd += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; catholics_spd += 2*(1-dissent) if spd_states

We campaign across the East, from Rostock to the Erzgebirge. [? if spd_states : Our minister-presidents in Brandenburg and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania help. ?]
